Z||000006||FieroKyle||09-07-2001||11:31 PM||||What did the T-birds run? a 4-cyl turbo? I know a kid at school who has one and it says turbo coupe on the back. He is a real ******* , he pulled out in front of me and flipped me so i rode his ass all the way to school, wish I had my buick, I would have rammed his ass and he would of got the ticket. Anyways, he started giving gas till he had it matted and passing cars at like 90. So I kept up on his ass (4 foot) with more gas to go and he couldn't lose me. So I figure they are a slow car.||||reg||8
Z||000007||fierospeeder||09-08-2001||01:42 AM||||the 87 and the 88 were the fastest tbirds.<BR>Came with an intercooler and averaged about 15psi stock.  You can increase the boost to 17.<P>The stickshift tbirds had 190hp while the auto's (which i own) had only 150.  The reason is a milder cam, and i cant be sure but i think the boost was a tad less.<P>In 87, it was the 4th fastest american production car.  Motortrend magazine of 87.  Vette was first, mustang/camero, then the tbird.    Tbirds top speed 144mph! that was the stick.<P>The tbird weighs 3415lbs so its close to lincolns weight.<P>2.3l turbo engine, 2 valves per cylinder<BR>8:1 compression<BR>mpefi injection<BR>1/4mile 16.3 seconds @ 84.5 mph<BR>60 - 0 mph stopping dist  138 ft.<BR>.82 lateral Gs<BR>700ft slalom  average 61.2mph<BR>0-60mph 8.5 seconds.<P>The sticks are a fast car and its pretty quick for a heavy car.  I kept up with a guy who owned a mark VIII i think, and he was about a car length ahead.  Its no v8 but once you modifiy the engine, its going to be a fast car.<P>Its a kewl car, abs brakes, automatic suspension, leather option plus sunroof, i have keyless entry.  Its awesome on curves and feels really safe, only sucks in the winter time, adding some weight in the back helps with traction<P>heres my pic of my car, its an old webpage i never finished<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierospeeder/ThunderbirdTurbo/thunderbird.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierospeeder/ThunderbirdTurbo/thunderbird.html</A> <P>one guy put in a v8 with twin superchargers.  His can do a wheely now.  I went along with his project from the start when he had his webpage.  He was in hotrod magazine about 2 months ago.  If i find the link i will post it.  <P>the SVO mustangs had 2.3l turbos but no intercoolers but they are freaking fast.  And when you mod them up they are 10-12 seconds 1/4 mile.  2.3l are strong motors.<P>check this site out what you can do with a 2.3l motor with more then 500hp. <A HREF="http://www.rbmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rbmotorsports.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||deceler8||09-08-2001||10:39 AM||||Some of the Mark VII's had a turbodiesel engine as an option (made by BMW).<P>Very few were sold, and BMW reportedly stopped selling the engine to Ford when Lincoln advertising started to target BMW and their claim as the "ultimate driving machine".<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
